        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>Zhongshan Lu (Road), the Bund Shanghai.\n</p><p>Built 1925, the former Nissin (Nihsin) Navigation Co. Building.\n</p><p>&lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.chinese-architecture.info/BUND/SH-BU-004.htm\">http://www.chinese-architecture.info/BUND/SH-BU-004.htm</a>\" rel=\"nofollow\"&gt;www.chinese-architecture.info/BUND/SH-BU-004.htm&lt;/a&gt;\n</p><p>xxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n</p><p>The Bund refers to the embankment area in central Shanghai that was the Shanghai International Settlement, where Western nations enjoyed speical powers and privileges in China.\n</p><p>As much as it's a shameful part of Chinese history, the legacy of the Bund is its historic Western-influenced buildings and wharves, which used to house many great banks, trading houses, insurance companies, shipping lines, newspapers and lawyer's offices.\n</p><p>&lt;a href=\"<a class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bund\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bund\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bund</a>\" rel=\"nofollow\"&gt;en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bund&lt;/a&gt;\n</p>\n&lt;a href=\"<a class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_International_Settlement\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_International_Settlement\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_International_Settlement</a>\" rel=\"nofollow\"&gt;en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_International_Settlement&lt;/a&gt;",
